# Under Camouflage each creature in a pile blocks the attacker the pile went to if it can (CR 509.1b): the blocks the piles
# make must still be a legal set together, so where the restrictions on the whole forbid some of them, as many are made as
# can be (CR 509.1c), the defending player choosing which. The first pile (the die's face 1) goes to Ravine Raider, which
# has menace (CR 702.111b): Phyrexian Walker alone in it can't block it. The second goes to Memnite, which Alpha Authority
# lets no more than one creature block (CR 509.1b): of the two Kobolds in it one blocks, and Bot2 is asked which - not none, not both,
# not a creature from the other pile, not the lone Walker against the Raider.
[Bot1 Deck]
Camouflage
Alpha Authority
Black Lotus
Swamp
Forest
Ravine Raider
Memnite
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Phyrexian Walker
Kobolds of Kher Keep
Crimson Kobolds
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

[Dice]
1

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ravine Raider.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Phyrexian Walker.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Kobolds of Kher Keep.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Crimson Kobolds.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Alpha Authority.Cast(Memnite)
Bot1.Attack(Ravine Raider > Bot2; Memnite > Bot2)
Bot1.Hand.Camouflage.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Choose(Phyrexian Walker)
Bot2.Choose(Kobolds of Kher Keep; Crimson Kobolds)
! Bot2.Block(Kobolds of Kher Keep > Memnite; Crimson Kobolds > Memnite)
! Bot2.Block(Phyrexian Walker > Ravine Raider)
! Bot2.Block(Phyrexian Walker > Memnite)
! Bot2.Block(Count: 0)
Bot2.Block(Crimson Kobolds > Memnite)
? Combat.Blocks = Crimson Kobolds > Memnite
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Graveyard = Crimson Kobolds
